# Genesis transfer switch
#
# Changing this file triggers .github/workflows/genesis-transfer.yml, which moves the cfb
# schema from the previous project into AIP2 and verifies all 46 table counts.
#
# The transfer is idempotent in the sense that it can be re-run, but a re-run restores over
# an already-populated schema and pg_restore will report "already exists" errors for every
# object. Re-run only deliberately, and read the count table at the end — that is the gate.

run: 2
requested-by: clyde
reason: >-
  genesis Job 2, second attempt. Run 1 aborted at pg_dump ("server version mismatch",
  client 16.14 vs server 17.6) and the job still reported success, because the step piped
  the script through tee under `bash -e` without `pipefail` and took tee's exit code.
  Nothing was restored. Both bugs are fixed: .github/actions/pg17 pins and verifies the
  17 binaries, and the step now sets pipefail.
